   156|            This reading is offered for self-reflection and symbolic guidance. It is not a substitute for professional legal, medical, financial, or health advice.
   157|        </div>
   158|    </div>
   159|
   160|    <div class="page">
   161|        <h2>Your Core Reading</h2>
   162|        <p>
   163|            Your Day Master is <span class="red-ink">Ren Water</span>. In practical terms, this suggests a person who reads patterns well, adapts quickly, and often thinks several steps ahead. The chart favors perception and strategy, but it may need help with confidence, warmth, and grounded follow-through.
   164|        </p>
   165|
   166|        <div class="highlight-box">
   167|            <strong>Core identity:</strong> thoughtful, intuitive, observant, and mentally agile. This is a chart that tends to understand the room before the room understands itself.
   168|        </div>
   169|
   170|        <h2>Four Pillars Summary</h2>
   171|        <table class="pillars-table">
   172|            <tr>
   173|                <th>Year</th>
   174|                <th>Month</th>
   175|                <th>Day</th>
   176|                <th>Hour</th>
   177|            </tr>
   178|            <tr>
   179|                <td>Geng Wu<br><small>Metal Horse</small></td>
   180|                <td>Xin Si<br><small>Metal Snake</small></td>
   181|                <td>Ren Chen<br><small>Water Dragon</small></td>
   182|                <td>Gui Mao<br><small>Water Rabbit</small></td>
   183|            </tr>
   184|        </table>
   185|
   186|        <h2>Elemental Balance</h2>
   187|        <table class="element-table">
   188|            <tr><th>Element</th><th>Strength</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
   189|            <tr><td><strong>Water</strong></td><td><span class="red-ink">Strong</span></td><td>Intuition, adaptability, mental depth</td></tr>
   190|            <tr><td><strong>Metal</strong></td><td>Moderate</td><td>Clarity, precision, discernment</td></tr>
   191|            <tr><td><strong>Wood</strong></td><td>Moderate</td><td>Growth, ideas, expansion</td></tr>
   192|            <tr><td><strong>Fire</strong></td><td><span class="red-ink">Weak</span></td><td>Visibility, expression, momentum</td></tr>
   193|            <tr><td><strong>Earth</strong></td><td><span class="red-ink">Weak</span></td><td>Stability, structure, completion</td></tr>
   194|        </table>
   195|
   196|        <div class="highlight-box">
   197|            <strong>Key insight:</strong> this chart does not need more sensitivity. It benefits more from support that strengthens confidence, steadiness, and visible action.
   198|        </div>
   199|
   200|        <h2>Recommended Jewelry Direction</h2>
   201|        <div class="jewelry-box">
   202|            <p><strong>Recommended plan:</strong> Career and Allies</p>
   203|            <p><strong>Suggested carrier:</strong> <span id="focusCarrier">Bracelet</span></p>
   204|            <p><strong>Suggested materials:</strong> <span id="focusMaterial">tiger eye, citrine, warm amber-toned stones, or a grounding Earth-Fire combination</span></p>
   205|            <p><strong>Reading logic:</strong> <span id="focusReason">the chart benefits from energy that helps the client be seen, trusted, and more consistent in execution.</span></p>
   206|        </div>
   207|
   208|        <h2>2026 Forecast</h2>
   209|        <p id="focusForecast">
   210|            The year 2026, the Year of the Fire Horse, is a more visible year for this chart. It favors speaking, publishing, asking for recognition, and stepping into the public side of work rather than staying only in the background.
   211|        </p>
   212|        <ul style="margin-left: 20pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;">
   213|            <li><strong>Career:</strong> stronger chances to be noticed</li>
   214|            <li><strong>Wealth:</strong> better returns from personal expertise than routine effort</li>
   215|            <li><strong>Relationships:</strong> more social movement, but quality still matters more than quantity</li>
   216|            <li><strong>Health:</strong> avoid burnout from mental overactivity</li>
   217|        </ul>
   218|
   219|        <div class="upgrade-banner no-print">
   220|            <h3>Order the Matching Jewelry Plan</h3>
   221|            <p>The report explains the direction. The bracelet or pendant turns that direction into a physical item that can be worn, confirmed, and shipped.</p>
   222|            <a href="checkout.html" class="cta-link">Choose My Jewelry Plan</a>
   223|        </div>
   224|
   225|        <div class="highlight-box">
   226|            <strong>A Closing Word from the Lineage:</strong> <span id="lineageClosing">The old readers do not fear a difficult chart, nor do they flatter an easy one. They look to what should be restrained, what should be nourished, and what should be carried close to the body so that the person's path may become more settled. What is shown here is only a brief opening. The fuller reading is where the hidden turns of the chart are judged with greater care.</span>
   227|        </div>
   228|
   229|        <div style="margin-top: 30pt; font-size: 9pt; color: #777; border-top: 1px solid #ddd; padding-top: 12pt;">
   230|            <strong>Disclaimer:</strong> This reading is prepared in a client-friendly English format based on traditional Chinese metaphysical ideas. It is intended for self-reflection and symbolic guidance only.
   231|        </div>
