   202|    <div class="page cover">
   203|        <div class="mountain-seal">DAO</div>
   204|        <div class="premium-badge">Premium Consultation</div>
   205|        <h1>Personal Destiny Reading</h1>
   206|        <div class="subtitle">Complete Four Pillars analysis with symbolic product guidance</div>
   207|        <div class="meta">
   208|            <strong>Prepared for:</strong> Alex Chen<br>
   209|            <strong>Date of Birth:</strong> May 15, 1990 at 11:42 AM<br>
   210|            <strong>Birth Location:</strong> Los Angeles, California, USA<br>
   211|            <strong>Report Date:</strong> April 15, 2026
   212|        </div>
   213|        <div class="master-line">Prepared by Oriental Destiny Premium Reading Service</div>
   214|        <div class="disclaimer">
   215|            This reading is offered for self-reflection, symbolic interpretation, and personal meaning. It is not a substitute for professional medical, legal, financial, or mental health advice.
   216|        </div>
   217|    </div>
   218|
   219|    <div class="page">
   220|        <div class="section-header">From the Reader</div>
   221|        <h2>Opening Counsel</h2>
   222|        <p>
   223|            A premium reading should feel thoughtful and human, not machine-generated. This version is written for overseas clients in clear English while preserving the symbolic language that gives BaZi and Feng Shui their depth.
   224|        </p>
   225|        <p>
   226|            The chart points to a person with strong Water and Metal qualities: perceptive, strategic, and mentally quick. The challenge is not insight. The challenge is how to make insight visible, practical, and steady in the outside world.
   227|        </p>
   228|
   229|        <div class="master-note">
   230|            <div class="master-note-header">Senior Reader's Note</div>
   231|            <p>Your Day Master is <span class="red-ink">Ren Water</span>. This is a chart that understands flow, nuance, and timing. It performs best when paired with stronger Fire for presence and stronger Earth for structure.</p>
   232|        </div>
   233|
   234|        <div class="signature-block">
   235|            <div class="signature-name">Your Oriental Destiny Senior Reader</div>
   236|            <div class="signature-title">Premium Consultation</div>
   237|        </div>
   238|    </div>
   239|
   240|    <div class="page">
   241|        <div class="section-header">Chart Structure</div>
   242|        <div class="chapter-title">Four Pillars and Elemental Logic</div>
   243|        <table class="pillars-table">
   244|            <tr>
   245|                <th>Year Pillar</th>
   246|                <th>Month Pillar</th>
   247|                <th>Day Pillar</th>
   248|                <th>Hour Pillar</th>
   249|            </tr>
   250|            <tr>
   251|                <td>Geng Wu / Metal Horse</td>
   252|                <td>Xin Si / Metal Snake</td>
   253|                <td>Ren Chen / Water Dragon</td>
   254|                <td>Gui Mao / Water Rabbit</td>
   255|            </tr>
   256|        </table>
   257|
   258|        <p>
   259|            The chart shows a mind-led nature with strong interpretive ability. Water gives sensitivity and adaptability. Metal gives discernment and edge. The weaker Fire and Earth suggest a need for warmth, momentum, consistency, and containment.
   260|        </p>
   261|
   262|        <div class="handwritten-box">
   263|            In modern language: this client does not need more ideas. The client needs support for confidence, completion, and a more visible presence in work and relationships.
   264|        </div>
   265|
   266|        <h3>Practical Reading</h3>
   267|        <ul>
   268|            <li><strong>Strength:</strong> high pattern recognition, strong intuition, useful judgment</li>
   269|            <li><strong>Risk:</strong> overthinking, delayed action, taking on too much emotional atmosphere</li>
   270|            <li><strong>Useful support:</strong> warmer, steadier, more grounded symbolic choices</li>
   271|        </ul>
   272|    </div>
   273|
   274|    <div class="page">
   275|        <div class="section-header">Product Guidance</div>
   276|        <div class="chapter-title">Recommended Jewelry Match</div>
   277|        <p>
   278|            This section is where the physical product becomes credible. Rather than selling random stones, the report explains why a particular carrier, material family, and symbol suit the client.
   279|        </p>
   280|
   281|        <div class="jewelry-box">
